00:05:05.799 --> 00:05:10.480
I want to start with the two anecdotes.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:15.480
One is the personnel and
it concerns my youth.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:21.360
When I was a 14, my
father basically sent me,

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:26.970
during the summer send me to work

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:31.850
in the small factory, in my village.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:36.850
And after a couple of days, I was there,

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.780
I was looking at my watch,

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:44.210
because it was 4:30 almost 5:00 PM.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.850
At 5:00 PM is the working days over,

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:50.520
I was looking for that time.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:55.520
And then another worker, colleague
look at me and he told me

00:05:57.587 --> 00:05:58.643
"What are you doing?

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.373
"Put your watch back into your pocket.

00:06:03.387 --> 00:06:06.807
"If the boss sees you that
you are looking at your watch,

00:06:06.807 --> 00:06:11.160
"he starts screaming like crazy."

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.400
I said, "Oh, wow."

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.120
And it was my second day.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.440
I'm like, well, it was the 14.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.943
And the the second anecdote,

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:25.870
is about another guy whose
name is Good Channel.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:30.390
And once he had the to introduce himself,

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.120
and he was a real factory worker.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.713
For me was just the
experience over one summer.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:44.520
And he introduced himself
by saying, "I have worked

00:06:45.277 --> 00:06:49.070
"for 30 years in that factory."

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:52.863
Then is he silent himself,

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.373
I think that life is not
just a second, sorry.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:01.733
I'm very sorry for that.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:10.670
And then he said, "Actually
it's not that I worked,"

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:16.683
actually he said "I have
been worked, for 30 years."

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:23.950
So why did I start with
these two anecdotes?

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:29.350
Because the first one
it show me, at that time

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.480
I couldn't understand
exactly what was going on.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.753
But the first time about
looking at my watch,

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.440
it shows me what, that
the time when you are

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.763
in the factory time doesn't belong to you.

00:07:49.472 --> 00:07:52.693
And the second example,
the second anecdote,

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:58.603
the body that has been worked.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:05.680
It shows that even the body
may be doesn't belong to you.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.113
So when you are a factory worker,

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:16.870
you sell your labor power,
but unfortunately for you

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:22.553
your body is attached to
that commodity labor power.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:28.740
And at that point, even the
body is not really yours.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:36.570
You have to be subjected to
a very specific discipline,

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:40.320
and not only is very often,
you have to be subjected

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:45.320
to a kind of a very noxious labor,

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:50.343
that really consumed your body.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.900
But in that second example

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.653
there even something more.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:02.440
Because in that transition from I worked,

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.920
in to, I have been worked,

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.893
I see the transition
from active to passive.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:18.020
And the passive form, that
is very present in capital

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:23.020
volume one, is very tricky,
because immediately,

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:31.740
forces us to think whose agency is that.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:37.080
When I say I have been
worked, who is the agent?

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:41.310
Whose agency is that?

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.650
So, and this is the starting
point of my presentation.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:50.650
I want to share my screen with you.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:01.450
So, when Marx wants to describe,
